  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Convection chances remain into early next week, then somewhat\nof a lull midweek before another front arrives late week. Some\nstorms into Sunday could be strong to severe with heavy\nrainfall.\n\nThe large scale pattern continues to show upper ridge to our\nsouthwest and trough over the northeast with convective\nperturbations moving from the Midwest east into the Ohio \nValley, then some upper flow/corfidi vectors track them across \nour area. \n\n\nThis afternoon/evening, outflows/differential heating will \ninfluence thunderstorm development. Shear will generally be \nweak, but strong updrafts and ample moisture will yield the \npotential for wet microbursts.\n\n\nNot much change in the forecast though looks less active Sunday\nwith ridge building a little more. As this happens, \ntemperatures will continue to rise, with near Heat Advisory \ncriteria levels possible across the Piedmont of Virginia and \nNorth Carolina on Sunday and Monday. By Monday evening the ridge\ngets flattened with more shortwaves moving across the area once\nagain. The flow being more westerly may keep storm coverage for\neast of the mountains somewhat limited.",
